  "id": "ex-12-modalverben-a1",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. The six modal verbs — können, müssen, wollen, sollen, dürfen, möchten (from mögen) — are all irregular in the singular (ich/er-sie-es have no ending and often a different vowel: ich kann, not ich könne) and always push the main verb to the end as a bare infinitive: Ich kann gut schwimmen. This set drills the forms first, then the meaning differences: können = ability, müssen = necessity, dürfen = permission, wollen = desire, sollen = someone else's expectation, möchten = a polite want. Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/12-modalverben-a1",
  "level": "A1",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Modalverben: Präsens und Bedeutung — A1",
  "topic": "Modalverben"
